<title>USA: TABLE-Deutsche Bank unit sells notes.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Deutsche Bank unit sells notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Deutsche Bank Financial Inc was priced Tuesday according to sole manager Deutsche Morgan Grenfell.</p>
<p>The notes are guaranteed by Deutsche Bank AG.</p>
<p>The offering was increased to $200 million from an original size of $100 million, they added.</p>
<p>BORROWER DEUTSCHE BANK FINANCIAL INC</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	 COUPON ZERO	 MATURITY 7/18/2017</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 20.749  FIRST PAY DATE 1/18/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S AA1   YIELD 8.02 PCT    PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P AAA	     YTM/YTC	 CALLABLE NON-CALL TWO</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678 ))</p>
</text>
